  "source_caveat": "The U.S. Bureau of Economic Analysis itself publishes a public, downloadable GrossOutput.xlsx file from its official apps.bea.gov industry Release/XLS/GDPxInd path. A direct independent GitHub Actions retrieval on October 12 2026 matched 506,819 bytes and SHA-256 a5a88e808bd88c5b48d7c1f572acb4d9b113d0d753828ed8b45d8800c1eb1f46. Its annual TGO103-A source sheet is BEA Chain-Type Quantity Indexes for Gross Output by Industry, with index reference 2017=100 and September 30 2026 publication. Truck transportation industry line 44, original workbook row 52, reports 2017 through 2024 indices 100.000, 102.952, 102.398, 103.678, 109.538, 108.519, 107.307, 108.047. Separate same-workbook annual TGO104-A BEA gross output price indices, TGO105-A current-dollar millions, and TGO106-A 2017 chained-dollar millions provide source-internal price/quantity/nominal checks, but these are same-publisher distributions, not independent BEA survey replications. The 8.05 percent gross output rise is a broad NAICS 484 economic output measure, not BLS 4.02 percent sectoral output, the 1.18 percent illustrative Census/PPI revenue proxy, BEA GDP/value added, freight tonnage, paid freight invoice overcharges, legally recoverable cash or RETALLY serviceable TAM. The prior invalid API UserID result remains historically accurate, but the authenticated BEA first-party XLSX now resolves the numeric source gap without an API key. None of the eighteen independent real-customer pilot approvals is met; no customer data, contracts, payment recoveries, external communications or deployment actions have occurred.",
